<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siret</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siret is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suceava">Suceava</a> County, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> and on the river of the same name. In the fourteenth century it was one of the first centres of the Principality of Moldavia: a Catholic bishopric was founded there around 1371, and princes resided there before the court moved to Suceava in the time of Petru I.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siret.jpg" alt="Siret" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel Bărbuță · CC BY-SA 3.0 ro · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fosta_prim%C4%83rie_a_ora%C8%99ului_Siret.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
